# Every Arch package Garage installs, one per line.
#
# Format: whitespace-separated fields. Field 1 is the package name. Field 2, if
# present, is `critical`. Blank lines are ignored; `#` starts a comment, either
# on its own line or trailing after the fields.
#
# The `critical` flag marks the subset `garage doctor` checks by name. From the
# backend's DOCTOR_PACKAGES, which this replaces as the source of truth:
#
#   Named because losing one of these is a broken desktop rather than a missing
#   extra: the shell, the bar, the terminal, the idle and wallpaper daemons, the
#   linker that puts the configuration in place, and the two theme assets that
#   every toolkit config names by string. The full package set lives here and is
#   not duplicated in the doctor -- `garage update` re-runs this whole list
#   through pacman anyway, which is a better check than repeating it.
#
# So `critical` is deliberately a small subset, not a judgement that the rest is
# optional. Everything in this file is installed; only the flagged ones are
# additionally asserted present by the doctor.
#
# NOT here: the NVIDIA set (nvidia-open, nvidia-utils, egl-wayland,
# libva-nvidia-driver). Those are appended by bootstrap.sh only when lspci sees
# an NVIDIA device, which is a decision about the machine rather than a fact
# about Garage, so it stays in bootstrap logic instead of becoming a flag here.

# Build tooling and the linker that puts the configuration in place
base-devel
git
curl
stow                            critical
cmake
meson
cpio
pkgconf
linux-headers

# The compositor and its portals
hyprland
uwsm
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk

# The Hyprland session daemons
hypridle                        critical
hyprlock
hyprpaper                       critical
hyprpolkitagent
hyprsunset

# The shell surfaces: bar, launcher, terminal, login shell
quickshell                      critical
kitty                           critical
fish                            critical
fisher

# On-screen feedback, clipboard and media keys
brightnessctl
cliphist
wl-clipboard

# Screenshot and annotation
grim
slurp
satty
hyprpicker

# Networking and Bluetooth
networkmanager
bluez
bluez-utils

# Audio
pipewire
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pavucontrol
cava

# The file manager and everything its panes need
thunar
thunar-archive-plugin
thunar-media-tags-plugin
tumbler
catfish
file-roller
ffmpegthumbnailer
poppler-glib
gvfs
gvfs-smb

# Small GNOME apps wired up as the default handlers
gnome-text-editor
gnome-calculator
loupe

# Terminal utilities and the Qt bridge
btop
fastfetch
micro
qt6ct
qt6-wayland
xsettingsd

# Scripting runtimes the backend and its helpers call
python
python-pip
python-pipx
uv
lua
jq
zenity
file
libnotify
7zip

# Theme assets every toolkit config names by string
papirus-icon-theme
adw-gtk-theme                   critical

# UI faces (Plus Jakarta Sans, Geist Mono) are bundled under
# desktop/.local/share/fonts, alongside Phosphor -- not Arch-packaged, and
# picked up by the post-stow fc-cache run in bootstrap.sh.
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-cjk
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-cascadia-mono-nerd
awesome-terminal-fonts

# The login manager and the hardware-facing utilities
remmina
freerdp
sddm
lm_sensors
xdg-user-dirs
desktop-file-utils
pciutils

# Desktop applications
spotify-launcher
discord
zed

# Containers
docker
docker-buildx
docker-compose

# JavaScript and TypeScript toolchain
nodejs
npm
pnpm
bun
deno
typescript-language-server
bash-language-server

# Rust toolchain
rustup
rust-analyzer

# Native toolchain and the profilers
clang
lldb
gdb
ninja
ccache
mold
valgrind
perf
strace

# Shell tooling and the fast CLI replacements
shellcheck
